	(text "inverting config\n-> for Rthevenin << Rfeedback : hysteresis-width ~ independant from treshold center\n-> source impedance does not influence thresholds\n\nwith 1.5V swing from photointerruptor we expect 3.3V (high) -> 1.8V (low)\n-> set center threshold to ~ 2.55V  \n-> currently: switching threshold: 2.42V, hysteresis: 240mV"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 329.184 24.892 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "337a7d7f-21af-4af3-b852-14137fc1133a")
	)
	(text "PD configured in Software to request fixed 12V profile"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 113.538 104.648 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(thickness 0.2381)
			)
			(justify right)
		)
		(uuid "356d4944-5a80-41aa-a2f6-b02072a9ee04")
	)
	(text "pin compatible with \nMCP6002\nTLV9062D"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.252 267.208 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "39c33760-798d-4879-a900-1268029b7e94")
	)
	(text "No CTR given\n\n1.)\nAt IF = 20mA -> Datasheet guaratees > 0.5mA photocurrent -> estimated worst case CTR ~0.5/20 = 2.5%\n-> worst case IC @ 10mA LED drive = 240µA\n-> For Rload = 1k -> Vlow,out = 3.3-240µA*1k = 3.1V -> only 0.2V swing\n\n2.)\nTo guarantee saturation in worst case, Rload must limit Ic to 240µA\nRload > (3.3-VCE,sat)/240µA = 13kOhm \n\n3.)\nEstimate Rload for large enough output swing:\nFor a swing of 2V -> Rload = 2/240µA = 8,3kOhm\n-> we want be rather fast, so try with a smaller Rload first\n\nhttps://josepheoff.github.io/posts/rpm"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.634 27.178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3e602468-1fea-4afa-81f0-88a957a4d3ea")
	)
